{"blocks": [{"bbox": [0.0, 0.0, 612.0, 792.0], "text": "", "type": "Page"}, {"bbox": [298.828125, 38.671875, 311.46435546875, 48.86529541015625], "text": "", "type": "PageHeader"}, {"bbox": [258.486328125, 53.665283203125, 353.6405944824219, 62.7852783203125], "text": "", "type": "PageHeader"}, {"bbox": [65.7421875, 93.5859375, 212.6439208984375, 136.8026123046875], "text": "half of people with a high school degree say they trust information from this source.", "type": "Text"}, {"bbox": [66.041015625, 157.0078125, 220.54896545410156, 296.9325866699219], "text": "Younger adults are also more likely to view information from the WHO as trustworthy; 68% of Americans ages 18 to 29 say they can trust information from the WHO at least a fair amount. Only about half of adults ages 65 and older (51%) share this view.", "type": "Text"}, {"bbox": [66.041015625, 317.49609375, 222.17333984375, 457.0325927734375], "text": "Differences by education and age, however, are relatively small compared with the substantial partisan division in these views. Conservative Republicans are much less likely than liberal Democrats to trust information coming from each international source.", "type": "Text"}, {"bbox": [65.7421875, 476.82421875, 222.4603271484375, 664.9425811767578], "text": "This partisan divide is especially pronounced on views about the WHO; 86% of liberal Democrats say they trust information from the WHO at least a fair amount, compared with 27% of conservative Republicans. Similar, though somewhat smaller, divisions also exist in trust in information from the EU and the Chinese government.", "type": "Text"}, {"bbox": [232.189453125, 99.44439697265625, 524.265869140625, 127.52435302734375], "text": "Younger adults and those with more education are more likely to trust information from the WHO", "type": "SectionHeader"}, {"bbox": [233.68359375, 134.51519775390625, 537.3394775390625, 155.63519287109375], "text": "% who trust information from the World Health Organization in regard to the coronavirus outbreak \u2026", "type": "Text"}, {"bbox": [233.2751319885254, 165.708984375, 541.8119804382325, 343.212890625], "text": "Not at all Not too much A fair amount A great deal Total 18% 22% 40% 20% Ages 18-29 11 19 42 25 30-49 16 22 42 19 50-64 20 22 39 18 65+ 26 23 34 16 Postgraduate 14 15 39 31 College grad 15 19 40 25 Some college 19 21 40 19 HS or less 20 26 39 14", "type": "Table"}, {"bbox": [233.31280593872071, 165.8822021484375, 293.7794960021973, 192.0380859375], "text": "", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [293.628800201416, 165.92550659179688, 359.4828651428223, 192.0380859375], "text": "Not at all", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [359.0307777404785, 165.8822021484375, 400.6228187561035, 192.0380859375], "text": "Not too much", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [400.5097969055176, 165.8822021484375, 470.8093879699707, 192.0380859375], "text": "A fair amount", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [470.8658988952637, 165.8822021484375, 541.6740882873535, 192.0380859375], "text": "A great deal", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [233.31280593872071, 191.84862899780273, 293.7794960021973, 208.72653579711914], "text": "Total", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [293.628800201416, 191.84862899780273, 359.4828651428223, 208.72653579711914], "text": "18%", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [359.0307777404785, 191.84862899780273, 400.6228187561035, 208.72653579711914], "text": "22%", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [400.5097969055176, 191.84862899780273, 470.8093879699707, 208.72653579711914], "text": "40%", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [470.8658988952637, 191.84862899780273, 541.5987403869628, 208.72653579711914], "text": "20%", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [233.31280593872071, 208.36386108398438, 293.7794960021973, 226.89816284179688], "text": "Ages 18-29", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [293.628800201416, 208.36386108398438, 359.4828651428223, 226.89816284179688], "text": "11", "type": "TableCell"}, {"bbox": [359.0307777404785, 208.36386108398438, 400.6228187